{"resourceIdentifier":"448","resourceName":"Methane Capture and Destruction at Simplot's Moses Lake Wastewater Treatment Facility","description":"The project involves the capture and destruction of biogas from a wastewater treatment operation at the JR Simplot Company (Simplot) processing plant in Moses Lake, Washington. The project is owned and operated by Simplot. The project activity consists of two stages. Stage 1 of the emission reduction project consists of the operation of a low rate anaerobic reactor (LRAR) installed in 2007. The captured biogas is flared during this stage. Stage 2 of the project involves the implementation of a biogas-to-boiler project. The captured biogas is transported to Simplot's adjacent potato processing facility for use in the facility's boilers, thereby displacing natural gas. To date, required piping has been installed to transport the biogas from the digester to the boiler, but the boiler has not yet been modified to use the biogas. This stage of the project is expected to be operational by late 2009.","location":{"latitude":47.127500,"longitude":-119.156944},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"448"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"WA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"J.R. Simplot Company"},{"type":"string","value":"São Paulo, Brazil"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"448"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"15851"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0014"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"0 Acres"}]},{"code":"VALIDATO